  "preamble": "Change of a palatalized voiced labial stop [bʲ] into a voiced palatal affricate [dʑ] ~ [dʒ]. The labial closure is lost and the palatal glide becomes a stop-plus-fricative. It is regular in the East Bodish languages of Bhutan: Proto-Bodish *bʲ (Classical Tibetan by-) shows up as j- in Kurtöp, Khengkha and Bumthang, while Dzala has the fricative zh-.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Affrication, Palatalization, Loss of Labial Articulation",
